    {
      "role": "MAIN",
      "node": {
        "id": 187029,
        "name": {
          "full": "Irene  Holton",
          "native": "아이린 홀튼",
          "alternative": [
            "King of Bankruptcy",
            "Monarch of Destitution",
            "アイリーン・ ホルトン"
          ]
        },
        "image": {
          "large": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b187029-dzi7JIAfPrVz.jpg"
        },
        "description": "Irene Holton is the only daughter of the Holton Family. She was known as the Monarch of Destitution. Irene is an innocent girl that is at first reluctant to do anything. During the fight against the relic Hand of Midas, with the help of Seo Joo-Heon, she gained confidence and dominated the relic and seized complete control over it. After this event, she would gain more confidence and start to help Seo Joo-Heon in his every task.",
        "gender": "Female",
        "age": null
      },
      "voiceActors": [
        {
          "id": 95869,
          "name": {
            "full": "Saori Hayami",
            "native": "早見沙織"
          },
          "image": {
            "large": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/staff/large/n95869-qCQ0EaWpq1QT.png"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "MAIN",
      "node": {
        "id": 187178,
        "name": {
          "full": "Jae-Ha Yu",
          "native": "유재하",
          "alternative": [
            "Monarch of Fraud",
            "Pushover Swindler",
            "Expert Pushover"
          ]
        },
        "image": {
          "large": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b187178-COovUjQPR7lr.png"
        },
        "description": "Before the time rewind, he was (and still is) a specialist in relic restoration. He became known as the Fraud King, something which Chairman Kwon eventually became aware of. Jae-Ha met Joo-Heon through being on the same raiding team.\n\n~!When Joo-Heon tries to seek him out in order to repair his relics, Irene informs him that he is 'dead'. She then recounts that he had sold her brother, George Hilton, a false painting. He was caught for the fraud and was presumed dead after his car fell down a cliff.He's later discovered to be alive when Edward called him on behalf of Chairman Kwon. Since he'd damaged his relic and needed it to be repaired. Something he agrees to.\n\nJoo-Heon lures him out by requesting a relic restoration. His high-ranking relics making Jae-Ha try to scam him with false ones, running away with the real ones. He fails to do so, being caught by Joo-Heon's rope relic.\n\nHe is then approached to sign a 'slave contract' which is then reformed to an 'exclusive contract'. In order to rope him in, Joo-Heon offers an explanation for how Richard Chang (his tutor) stole Jae-Ha's art style. In addition to giving him back the elements of art and reputation that Richard had stolen from him.!~\n\n",
        "gender": "Male",
        "age": null
      },
      "voiceActors": [
